From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DroidDeck Mali <noreply@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:59:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] android: route plain renameat2 through renameat

Android's app seccomp policy can return ENOSYS for renameat2 before the host
kernel executes it. Steam's updater uses renameat2 with flags=0 for ordinary
backup renames and then loops forever applying the update.

After PRoot has translated both paths, replace only the flags=0 form with
renameat. The first four arguments are ABI-compatible, Android permits renameat,
and PRoot already translates it. Advanced renameat2 operations remain untouched.
---
 src/syscall/enter.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/syscall/enter.c b/src/syscall/enter.c
index b84fdc3..1111111 100644
--- a/src/syscall/enter.c
+++ b/src/syscall/enter.c
@@ -568,8 +568,14 @@ int translate_syscall_enter(Tracee *tracee)
 		if (status < 0)
 			break;
 
 		status = translate_path2(tracee, newdirfd, newpath, SYSARG_4, SYMLINK);
+		if (status < 0)
+			break;
+
+		if (syscall_number == PR_renameat2
+		    && peek_reg(tracee, CURRENT, SYSARG_5) == 0)
+			set_sysnum(tracee, PR_renameat);
+
 		break;
 
 	case PR_symlink:
